===History===
{{rfc-header|History|lang=en}}
The history of Skeeze began in the mid 00's, when K2 Skis released its first full publication of a newschool skiing magazine titled 'SKEEZE'.  The title 'SKEEZE" derived from a slang term for 'Skis' and also referenced a former newschool publication called 'FREEZE'.  'FREEZE' had stopped all publishing several years before, and this had been a huge loss to the skiing community.  As an ode to its fallen comrade, the team at K2 Skis produced SKEEZE for the first time in 2004.  The publication was in print for 3 years, and gradually developed into an annual team video that was distributed globally to shops and dealers associated with K2 Skis.  Segments from these many SKEEZE movies can still be found on YouTube, and were primarily responsible for shaping modern day skiing as we know it.  Today, SKEEZE has evolved once more into a viral media website that distributes and produces some of the most revolutionary and insightful content within the ski industry.

